// error — what the library raises when the platform refuses.
//
// One root, so a game that does not care which call failed writes a
// single `catch e : PlatformError`, and one that does reads `e.message`.
// The failure is in the *type of the function that failed*, not in a
// global to be read afterwards — which is what makes it impossible to
// forget to check and impossible to read the wrong call's answer.
//
// Only *recoverable* failures come through here — a display that cannot
// be opened, a window the desktop refused. An allocation that the
// process cannot satisfy is not one of those: `Blob` aborts instead of
// threading an out-of-memory branch through every caller.

/** A platform call the library depends on did not succeed. */
pub exception PlatformError {
    /** Carry the failing call and what it reported. */
    constructor(message : string) {
        super(message);
    }
}
